# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Config, not content.
#
# Pages already serves HTML as max-age=0, must-revalidate, but everything else
# defaults to four hours. That skew is worse than plain staleness: the browser
# fetches fresh markup and pairs it with a stylesheet from four hours ago, so a
# layout change renders with the old rules and the page looks broken rather
# than merely out of date. HTML and CSS are deployed together and have to
# expire together.
#
# The cost is a conditional GET on a 2.7 KB gzipped file, which almost always
# answers 304. Images keep the default: they are large, they change rarely, and
# a stale one is only ever a stale picture.
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
